    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 203.3204441713483
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " Player. finish now stops the player before releasing it, so replacement and explicit stop do the same thing instead of one leaning on ARC timing. That made stop() collapse to  ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 217.67265405547744
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " a single finish(.success(.interrupted)) — the symmetry the reviewer wanted, one line shorter than before. Verified by driving real audio in the dev app: clicking row one's     ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 232.0248639396067
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " waveform shows the stop glyph on that row alone; clicking row two's while it plays moves the stop glyph to row two and returns row one to a waveform, so the replacement path   ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 246.37707382373594
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " runs through the actor and settles correctly.                                                                                                                                   ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 260.7292837078651
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : "                                                                                                                                                                                 ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 275.08149359199433
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " Documentation. The reviewer is right that the rule and the code couldn't both stand as written. The amendment narrows the constraint to what it actually covers rather than     ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 289.4337034761236
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " softening it: a value-scoped .animation on the row is still ignored for an async change, but on a leaf view inside the row it works, because animating a child's opacity        ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 303.7859133602527
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " resolves inside the row's own body instead of the transaction List hands its rows. That line is the whole rule. withAnimation at the mutation site stays documented as the      ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 318.138123244382
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " fallback for anything the row animates as a whole, and the leaf spelling is now the preferred one where it applies, since it keeps presentation timing out of the reducer.      ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 332.4903331285112
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : "                                                                                                                                                                                 ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 346.84254301264036
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " I added the value-dependent animation idiom to the skill too — isCopied ? nil : .easeOut(duration: 0.5) — since that's how one piece of state gets instant arrival and slow     ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 361.1947528967696
  },
  {
    "height" : 14.352209884129213,
    "role" : "AXTextArea",
    "text" : " exit, and it's the thing that let the two-case enum die.                                                                                                                        ",
    "web" : false,
    "width" : 1259,
    "x" : 0,
    "y" : 375.54696278089887
  },
